  "result": "All 8 tests pass (5 existing, 3 new). The SPEC's public-interface section is described as fixed, so I'll leave it untouched.\n\n**What I changed** (all in `kvstore/store.py`):\n\n- **On-disk layout** is now a nested JSON object, `{namespace: {key: value}}`, still in the one data file. Files written in the old flat `{key: value}` layout are migrated into the `default` namespace on load, so existing data keeps working.\n- **`set`, `get`, `delete`, `keys`** each take a keyword argument `ns: str = \"default\"` and operate only within that namespace.\n- **New `count(ns=\"default\")`** returns the number of keys in a namespace, and **new `namespaces()`** returns the sorted names of namespaces that hold at least one key.\n- **Empty namespaces are pruned.** Deleting the last key in a namespace removes it from the document, so a namespace never lingers with zero keys and `namespaces()` stays accurate after deletes and across reopen.\n- Loading validates the nested shape and rejects non-string keys or values, as before.\n\nI also verified by hand that a legacy flat file migrates correctly and that only the single data file is ever written. Nothing was committed.",
